                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7f1b210a-d9d9-336d-98d6-a2abf7586902",
                        "entry_id": "2932b5eb-d9fb-3ab3-894c-559babc31b6a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ботан., рег. полынь, травянистое растение семейства сложноцветных с пряным запахом"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cab39ee3-3db6-4227-bdce-f226995c40e7",
                                "sense_id": "7f1b210a-d9d9-336d-98d6-a2abf7586902",
                                "text": "Полынь полевая, или чернобыль, чернобыльник, нехворощь, А. campestris L., встречается весьма часто на каменистых и пустынных местах."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "19ddf18c-505f-355b-b65f-0a4d23e57f5a",
                        "entry_id": "2932b5eb-d9fb-3ab3-894c-559babc31b6a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "рег. живая насадка для рыбалки, гусеница, зимующая в сухих стеблях полыни"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e646895-6b99-466b-80d2-27d73ac7fcf4",
                                "sense_id": "19ddf18c-505f-355b-b65f-0a4d23e57f5a",
                                "text": "Кто прав, кто нет, пусть решают биологи, но рыба различия между репейником и чернобыльником не делает, клюет и на того и на другого одинаково хорошо."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "22daeaa2-6f16-4dd0-8dd1-d6b485bb8ad0",
                        "source_entry_id": "2932b5eb-d9fb-3ab3-894c-559babc31b6a",
                        "target_lang_word": "mugwort",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mugwort",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "06662e7b-3fb8-3f79-9145-4573551449bf",
                                        "entry_id": "bf5467a8-2546-3074-99cd-2ab0e23659d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several aromatic plants of the genus Artemisia native to Europe and Asia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5fa7e54e-c78f-3b0a-8613-59c30d31ed5e",
                                        "entry_id": "bf5467a8-2546-3074-99cd-2ab0e23659d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Artemisia vulgaris, traditionally used medicinally."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d6e2ccd-04aa-48b8-9668-df0cd8674b0a",
                                                "sense_id": "5fa7e54e-c78f-3b0a-8613-59c30d31ed5e",
                                                "text": "Mugwort is with good success put among other herbs that are boiled, for women to sit over the hot decoction to draw down their courses, to help the delivery of the birth and expel the afterbirth, as also for the obstructions and inflammations of the mother."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4097eb9a-bf9b-4c4f-bc8c-1066d7564a62",
                                                "sense_id": "5fa7e54e-c78f-3b0a-8613-59c30d31ed5e",
                                                "text": "Peony would keep away any kind of storms. Mugwort hung over doorways on Midsummer's Day, June 24, would keep off lightning, as St. John's-Wort would if gathered before sunrise on that day."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
